# Client Architecture

Condensed from `client/CLAUDE.md` (full source of truth). When in doubt, extract to the correct layer.

## One-way dependencies

```
pages  ──▶  features  ──▶  shared
             (features may use shared; shared must NEVER import features)
```

```
src/
  app/            router, providers, queryClient, RouteError (wiring only)
  pages/          thin route entries — compose features + read route params only
  layout/         HubShell, ChatsLayout, AdminWrapper (app-wide presence/alerts OK here)
  features/<domain>/   auth · chat · whisper · hub · admin · profile · notifications · landing
      api/        HTTP helpers via shared api client (no logic/UI)
      components/  hooks/  stores/  utils/
      hooks/queryKeys.ts   ALL TanStack query keys for this domain
      types.ts    ALL domain data-model types (or types/)
      index.ts    PUBLIC API — the only thing other slices may import
  shared/         domain-agnostic ONLY
      components/  (ui/ icons/ charts/ skeletons/ media/ image-viewer/ sidebar/ tables/)
      hooks/  utils/  constants/   (app.ts, socket.ts)
      lib/         api/client.ts (fetch + cookies + 401 refresh), socket/
      types/       user.ts, icon.ts, media.ts, socket.ts, ui.ts, index.ts
  assets/  styles/  main.tsx
```

- No other top-level folders under `src/`. No feature code in `pages/`/`app/`/`layout/`.
- **`shared/` importing `@/features/...` is the #1 forbidden smell.**
- Cross-feature: `@/features/<domain>` (`index.ts`) only — never deep subpaths.
- **Inside a feature: relative imports only** (`./` / `../`). Never `@/features/<self>/…`.

## Thin pages

Pages compose feature components and read route params. No forms, mutations, domain toasts, or fetch orchestration in `pages/` — push into a feature hook/component.

## Separation of concerns

Components render JSX. Hooks decide. Utils compute (pure). Api fetches. Stores hold state.

| Concern | Where |
|---|---|
| Data fetching | `hooks/useXxxQueries.ts` (TanStack Query) |
| Mutations | `hooks/useXxxMutations.ts` |
| Derived UI logic | `hooks/useXxx.ts` |
| Pure transforms | `utils/…` (no toast/navigate/network/hooks) |
| HTTP calls | `features/<domain>/api/…` via `@/shared/lib/api/client` |
| Query keys | `hooks/queryKeys.ts` only — never inline `queryKey: ['…']` |
| Global client state | `stores/…` (zustand) |

No data fetching, `.then()` chains, or business logic in a component body — extract to a hook.

## One HTTP client

All backend calls go through `api` from `@/shared/lib/api/client` (fetch, cookies, refresh). Feature `api/*.ts` only wrap that client. Raw `fetch` only for non-API blobs/downloads. XHR only for upload progress (e.g. R2). Never add axios or a second API client.

## Query keys & ownership

- Define every key/factory in that feature's `hooks/queryKeys.ts`.
- Keys live with the **domain that owns the resource**. Session/profile keys belong under auth (or a shared keys module) — do not grow unrelated keys under chat. Other features invalidate via the owner's public API / exported factories.

## Types — strict placement

- Only type in a `.tsx`: its own `type Props = {…}` above the component.
- A hook `.ts` may have one private `interface Params {…}`.
- Domain models → `features/<domain>/types.ts` (or `types/`); shared → `shared/types/{ui,media,socket,user,icon}.ts`.
- Never export a reusable type from a component/hook file.

## Adding code

- **New feature** → needed folders + `types` + `hooks/queryKeys.ts` + `index.ts`; register route in `app/router.tsx` (lazy-load if heavy). New socket names → `shared/constants/socket.ts`.
- **New shared component** → `shared/components/<category>/`; local `Props`; never imports a feature.
